I go to a busy vegetable stall.
There are many vegetables there.
I see the fresh tomatoes.
They are very beautiful.
I point to the tomatoes.
I ask the vendor, "Brother, what is the price of one kilo of tomatoes?"
The vendor says, "Madam, one kilo is forty rupees."
I only want a little.
I say, "I want half a kilo."
"Please give me those."
The vendor weighs the tomatoes.
He puts them in my bag.
I ask, "What is the total price?"
He answers, "Twenty rupees."
I give him twenty rupees.
The vendor accepts the money and smiles.
I also smile and walk forward.
